# Live Graph Contract

**All audio mutations go through the live PipeWire graph.**  
The only intentional outsides are Tear down (recovery) and hard errors.

## Entry point

```rust
state.commit(LiveChange::…);
```

Defined in `app/src/audio/live.rs`. Maps to worker commands → `buschain-engine` intents.

## Engine first — no naked APIs

**Never** add `pactl` / `pw-link` / `pw-cli` / `pipewire` spawns under `app/`.

- New capability → extend `buschain_engine::contract::Intent` / `AudioBackend` in `engine/`.
- App uses `crate::audio::engine_handle` or worker `Command::BindMasterClock` / graph shim.
- See `engine/README.md` and `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`.

## Severity ladder

1. `Levels` / `Level` — volume/mute
2. `FxParams` — knobs / mix / **insert power** (Props on multi-node FX)
3. `FxRewire` — add/remove/reorder (respawn one `buschain_fx_*` + exclusive routes)
4. `EnsureTrack` / prune — one bus
5. `Route` — destination/input **links only** (never respawn FX)
6. `Reconcile` — idle ensure / cold bring-up / recovery
7. Tear down — **ERROR RECOVERY ONLY**

## Clock

- `GraphClock` = Master HW rate/quantum after Apply (`session.performance`).
- **DeviceCaps** from EnumFormat ∪ ALSA `Rates:` only — Custom dropdown ⊆ those rates (no phantom 192k).
- Config **Apply audio settings** → `BindMasterClock`: force-rate/quantum → wait HW running match → push BusChain props → tear bridges/posts → `ClockBind` ForceRespawn FX + exclusive mic rewire.
- Balanced Apply clears force-rate/quantum; Custom forces the selected capable rate.
- Soft quantum → `clock.force-quantum = 0` (PipeWire may raise period); hard quantum locks `node.force-quantum`.
- External rate mismatch → exclusive inbound `buschain_rs_*`; rest of chain stays at GraphClock. Never dual-path direct+bridge.
- Outbound Master→HW never rate-bridged.

## Sealed insert pipeline (engine owns the wire)

```
{bus}.monitor ──exclusive──► buschain_fx_{bus} (n0→n1→… black boxes)
                                     │
                                     ▼
                              buschain_post_{bus}   (meter tap)
                                     │
                                     ▼  arm only after ready + ~200ms dwell
                              Master / targets
                                     │
                              Master→HW (session barrier)
```

| Op | Engine intent | Forbidden |
|----|---------------|-----------|
| Power / knobs / mix | `PushFxControls` → Props (lock-free of Engine ensure) | Respawn; Mix-as-power; plugin-identity branches |
| Add / remove / reorder | Async `EnsureFxChain(Force)` + dry link + monitor gate + soft-cutover | Route/Hotplug ForceRespawn; audible dry/partial FX while Building; HOL Props thread |
| Cold bring-up / Full Apply | `ArmSession` (warm-adopt if graph already healthy) | App `pw-link` / last-resort dry while Building |
| Route (HW / targets) | `arm_track_egress` after Wet (+ dwell) | Dry bypass while Building; arm Master→HW in app |
| Mute / fader | Levels on outbound path | Mute/zero app-facing sink |

### End-to-end track arming

- **Building (ForceRespawn)**: keep dry `bus→dest` *link* (no cork) but **gate `{bus}.monitor`** so output is silent until the full wet rack is sealed; feed FX + hold. Soft-cutover arms `post→dest`, drops dry, then ungates monitor.
- **Dwell**: ~60ms continuous spine ready before arming wet egress (flap resets timer). Dry tracks use ~40ms existence check.
- **Session barrier**: on cold `ArmSession`, keep Master→HW disarmed until Master spine ready **and** every unmuted non-master insert track is `Wet` or `Failed` (Failed+dry = resolved). Latch `speakers_armed` so idle reconcile does not re-silence.
- **Warm adopt (UI restart)**: if live PW already matches Desired (buses, FX signature+spine, Master→HW), latch `speakers_armed` and Idempotent-reconcile — do **not** disarm or ForceRespawn. Fail closed → cold arm.
- **Failed ensure**: `restore_dry` then arm dry (fail-open). Does not block the barrier forever.
- App commits `DesiredState` + intents only — no naked disarm/arm via pactl/pw-link.

- New FX capability → `EnsureFxChain` / `PushFxControls` / `ArmSession` in `engine/` first.
- **Never** spawn `pipewire -c` or FX Props from `app/` — only `engine/backend/fx_chain.rs`.
- `engine.chain_state(bus)` is the single wet/dry/failed source of truth.
- v1: LADSPA inserts only (LV2/CLAP/VST3 scan stays; wiring waits on `InsertBackend`).
- Keepalive `{bus}.monitor → buschain_hold` always preserved during wet switch.
- Stereo: `channels=2`, `channel_map=front-left,front-right` on sinks.

## GraphSupervisor

`Engine::reconcile` owns continuous Desired↔live health (buses, levels, FX, preferred default). Master→HW repair only when `speakers_armed`. Cold Full Apply uses `ArmSession`. Idle worker ticks call `reconcile_light`. Nuclear reset is Config → Advanced only — never a primary UI verb.

## Hard rules

- Never move sink-inputs as a mixer side effect
- Cold graph → auto bring-up; never prompt “click Apply”
- Apps stay on `buschain_*` buses
- Level by `expected_sink_name` — never leave create-mute@0
- Never return happy dry when the insert rack is non-empty — surface `ChainState::Failed`
- Never mute the app-facing null-sink; never open egress before dwell / barrier

## Anti-patterns

```rust
// BAD — power rebuilds FX / PushFxParams → rewire_track_fx (YouTube pause)
state.schedule_fx_rewire(id); // for bypass
// BAD — mute {bus}.monitor or recreate buschain_track_* with apps attached
// BAD — spawn filter-chain from app/
std::process::Command::new("pipewire").args(["-c", …])

// GOOD — Props power
state.commit(LiveChange::FxParams { track_id }); // → PushFxControls

// GOOD — add/remove/reorder
state.commit(LiveChange::FxRewire { track_id }); // → EnsureFxChain(Force)

// GOOD — listen / HW out
state.commit(LiveChange::Route); // post→dest when Wet

// BAD — naked CLI in app
std::process::Command::new("pactl")…

// GOOD — engine intent
engine.apply(Intent::EnsureFxChain { … });
```
